# Wealth Partner App UX Constitution (CO-WP-103B)

Status: **PRODUCT OWNER DIRECTION** · Priority: **CRITICAL** · Governing principle for all WP App work  
Companion to: CO-WP-CONSTITUTION-001 · `enterprise-wealth-partner-app.mdc`

## Philosophy (non-negotiable)

The Wealth Partner App is **not**:

- a CRM
- a reporting application
- a dashboard / MIS
- a mobile version of Catalyst One

It is a **Daily Business Companion**.

Partners should **want** to open it multiple times per day.  
It inspires business generation — it does not display reports.

**Catalyst One runs the business. The Wealth Partner App helps the partner succeed.**

## Design principles

Every page must feel: Premium · Minimal · Elegant · Modern FinTech · Highly interactive.

- No dense tables
- No enterprise dashboard feeling
- No clutter
- Large cards · rounded corners · excellent spacing · beautiful gradients · meaningful animations

Reference spirit: Groww · CRED · Jupiter · Zerodha · PhonePe Business — never Salesforce-on-mobile.

## Morning test (mandatory)

Every new screen must answer:

> Would a Wealth Partner enjoy opening this every morning?

If **no** → redesign before shipping.

## Home page principle

Home is an **EXPERIENCE**, not an MIS.

Allowed on Home:

- Greeting
- Hero Carousel
- My Business Today (compact chips)
- Business Feed
- Recommended Actions
- Today's Highlights
- Digital Visiting Card
- Compact Saarthi

**Forbidden on Home:** pipeline statistics · deal counts · opportunity cards · commission cards · CRM KPI strips.

Those belong on **Business**.

Opening Home should feel: “What is happening today?” — never “How many customers do I have?”

## Enterprise Experience Engine

Assume every Home visual element is eventually driven by the **Enterprise Experience Engine** in Catalyst One:

Hero cards · Business Feed · Campaigns · Training · Marketing creatives · Announcements · Notifications · Quick Actions · Highlights · Digital Toolkit

Do **not** architect companion-local hardcoded business content as the long-term SSOT.  
Catalogues may temporarily seed Experience Engine projections in Catalyst One only — the app still only renders Partner API DTOs.

## Catalyst One decides · App renders

Catalyst One decides: who sees content · products · campaigns · notifications · quick actions · visiting card · professional title · training.

Wealth Partner App: presentation · navigation · session · device UX only.

